# Jachai News — Cursor project rules

You are working on **Jachai News**, a Bangladesh-focused news intelligence product: multi-source headline clusters, perspective/bias signals, rumor flags, and blindspot detection. Installable **PWA**; UI is English + Bangla where the app already uses both.

**Detailed rules** live in `.cursor/rules/` (`jachai-news.mdc` always applies; `backend.mdc` / `frontend.mdc` / `supabase.mdc` when editing those trees).

## Architecture

- `backend/` — Python 3.11+, FastAPI, async SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL, RSS ingestion (`app/services/rss_ingestion.py`), Groq/Gemini via `app/services/ai_client.py`; source seed in `app/data/bd_sources_seed.py`; `POST /api/v1/ingest` + `npm run ingest:backend`
- `frontend/` — Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, optional Supabase auth (`src/lib/supabase.ts`, `database.types.ts`, `/sign-in`, `/sign-up`)
- `supabase/` — migrations for profiles, Pro subscriptions, bKash records (news data stays in backend Postgres)
- Root scripts: `npm run dev:frontend`, `dev:backend`, `ingest:backend`
- **Admin ops (internal)**: backend `GET /api/v1/admin/overview` (`app/api/admin.py`, `admin_stats.py`); frontend password-gated `/admin` + `app/api/admin/*` (server-only `ADMIN_*` / `INGEST_API_KEY` — see `frontend.mdc`)
- **Monitoring (optional)**: Sentry on backend (`app/core/sentry_init.py`) and frontend (`@sentry/nextjs`, `instrumentation.ts`); ingest cron pings via `app/services/ops_alerts.py` (Healthchecks.io + Telegram when env is set)

## Conventions

### Backend
- Thin routes in `app/api/`; logic in `app/services/`; schemas in `app/schemas/`; models in `app/models/`
- Async for I/O; config in `app/core/config.py`; API prefix `/api/v1`; optional `INGEST_API_KEY` for ingest; never commit secrets

### Frontend
- Pages under `frontend/src/app/`; components in `src/components/`
- Fetch via `src/lib/api.ts` and `src/lib/stories.ts` (API + `demo-data.ts` fallback)
- Pro tier: `subscription-features.ts` (matrix), `subscription-access.ts` (`NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`), `subscription-plans.ts` (pricing); browse gated for free users
- Server components for feeds; client components for interactive meters/modals/tabs/PWA/theme

## Product vocabulary

- **Cluster / headline clash** — Same story, different framings
- **Perspective** — independent, neutral, establishment, opposition, international
- **Bias meter** — Scored lean for a source or cluster
- **Rumor badge** — Unverified or speculative coverage
- **Blindspot** — One-sided coverage on a story
- **Jachai Pro** — Free daily top 10 on home; full browse/archive and pro analytics locked behind Pro (see feature matrix)

## Quality bar

- Match existing layout and naming; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Type hints on Python public functions; strict TypeScript on frontend
